      ],
      "source": "https://www.stjoearkansas.org/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s original name was Monkey Run before it became St. Joe.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.stjoearkansas.org/History.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A 1920s‑era depot, restored to its early‑20th‑century look, still stands on U.S. Route 65 in St. Joe.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St._Joe%2C_Arkansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "St. Joe’s founding in 1860 by Bill Campbell and others placed it just north of the Buffalo River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.stjoearkansas.org/History.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The town’s historic buildings and the Rural Help Center reflect a revitalized pioneer spirit, turning St. Joe into a gateway to Buffalo River recreation.",
